  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2024-09-17T17:19:58.750Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "As mentioned in my [detailed feature request for this](https://feedback.vrchat.com/feature-requests/p/live-typing-mode-in-the-chatbox-for-reading-texts-in-real-time) a while back, I pointed out that having this feature able to be toggled easily so that it can be used 50% of the time is crucial to its implementation, in my opinion.\n\nI want to be able to choose if my texts appear in real time on a per-message basis by having access to a toggle in the keyboard itself. Having this option hidden in the main menu settings is extremely frustrating.\n\nHaving the toggle on the keyboard itself also shows to the user the way their chatbox is currently functioning, and won't create confusion when people aren't sure what mode they're on.",
